\c 26
\v 3 If you walk in my commands and observe my commandments and do them,
\v 4 then I shall give you the rain in its season; and the land will yield its produce, and the trees of the plains will yield their fruit.
\v 5 The time for you to thresh will overtake the vintage, and the vintage will overtake the sowing, and you will eat your bread and be replete and live in safety on your land; and war will not pass through your land.
\ 6 I shall grant peace in your land, and you will sleep with no one to fear; and I shall destroy the evil beasts from your land.
\ 7 You will put your enemies to flight, and they will fall slaughtered before you.
\ 8 Five of you will put to flight a hundred, and a hundred of you will put to flight tens of thousands, and your enemies will fall before you by the sword.
\v 9 I shall look upon you and increase and multiply you, and I shall establish my covenant with you.
\v 10 You will eat the old and the very old, and you will bring out the old, making way for the new.
\v 11 I shall pitch my tent among you, and my soul will not abhor you.
\v 12 And I shall walk among you and I shall be your God, and you will be my people.
\v 13 I am the Lord your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt when you were slaves, and I broke the bonds of your yoke and led you with boldness.
\v 14 But if you do not obey me nor observe these, my commandments,
\v 15 but disobey them with your soul angered by my judgements, so that you do not keep all my commandments and turn from my covenant,
\v 16 then I shall do so to you, and I shall bring distress upon you with itching and jaundice, and putrefaction in your eyes, so that your life wastes away. You will sow your seed in vain, and your enemies will eat it.
\v 17 I shall set my face against you, and you will fall before your enemies; those who hate you will put you to flight, and you will flee when no one pursues you.
\v 18 And if at this point you do not obey me, then I shall add to your punishment sevenfold
for your sins.
\v 19 I shall crush the arrogance of your pride, and I shall make your sky as iron and your earth like bronze.
\v 20 Your strength will be useless, and your land will not yield its seed, and the tree of your field will not yield its fruit.
\v 21 If after this you walk perversely and refuse to obey me, I shall bring another seven plagues in accordance with your sins.
\v 22 I shall send the savage beasts of the land against you, and they will devour you and consume your livestock; they will make you few in number, and your roads will be deserted.
\v 23 And if you are not chastened by these things, but walk perversely with me,
\v 24 then I too will walk perversely with you, and I too shall strike you seven times for your sins.
